{"author":{"id":"7c5527b9befade3b1be0c1d677ac996815288d8332f34269730a5b81425ee5be"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1791209086,"nonce":"LXF9RS7JEpAM/bhR8MT94rZgy+4=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"LE_lADOULtcMc8AAAABVIwS_88AAAAHkgzYdg","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:labels":"refactor"},"added":["refactor"],"removed":[]},{"type":6,"timestamp":1791272569,"nonce":"Tlv9dshxvO6CNmb7HyP6fVAzxiw=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"UCE_lAHOULtcMc8AAAABVIwS_87-YKU0","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"5fd30b28cfa1d560a1de008e04895da7547a351e8ce56056acae2ad5507665d0"},"target":"5df752cf713d8e95743a1a7d1a7d1d6b12fe1fa63fa308662f8ed6679d7f674a","message":"**TL;DR**\n- **What:** small code-health fixes.\n- **Why:** hard-coded texts can't be translated, the Scope icon is broken, and an undeclared library can disappear on install.\n- **User impact:** Scope icon fixed.\n- **Effort:** small.\n\n---\n\n**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\nA handful of smaller problems, each one cheap to fix:\n\n1. **`echarts` is used but not declared.** It is imported directly in `src/components/results/DatacentersPieChart.vue`, `EmbodiedTreemapChart.vue` and `TotalSplitPieChart.vue`, yet `package.json` only lists `vue-echarts`. It only works because npm installs `echarts` as a peer dependency.\n2. **`lefthook` is a runtime dependency.** It sits in `dependencies`, but it's a dev tool the app never imports.\n3. **Types have two import paths.** `src/models/mitsi.ts` re-exports the schema types \"so pages and components keep importing from `src/models/mitsi` exactly as before\". It's a compatibility layer: 9 files import from `models/mitsi`, 8 from `models/schema`.\n4. **Icon fonts instead of SVG.** `quasar.config.ts` loads `roboto-font`, `material-icons` and `material-symbols-rounded` for 7 icons (`menu`, `delete`, `restart_alt`, `bolt`, `dns`, `insights`, `scope`):\n   - `material-symbols-rounded` is unused, yet it adds a 5 MB woff2 to `dist/`;\n   - `scope` (the Scope nav item in `MainLayout.vue`) isn't a Material Icons name (`@quasar/extras` has no `matScope`), so that icon doesn't render properly;\n   - the team convention is SVG icons, no icon fonts.\n5. **Hard-coded strings sit next to i18n.** All user-facing text should go through i18n:\n   - `TotalSplitPieChart.vue` falls back to `'Underlying services'` (this goes away with #41);\n   - `MainLayout.vue` hard-codes `alt=\"EPFL\"` and the brand text `MITSI`;\n   - `formatKg` in `src/utils/format.ts` hard-codes `Intl.NumberFormat('en-US')`, while the app's locale comes from vue-i18n (`en`, messages in `en-GB`), so number formatting ignores the i18n locale;\n   - `scopeFuDuration` and `scopeFuResourceCount` in `src/i18n/en-GB/index.ts` are never used.\n\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\n- [ ] Add `echarts` to `dependencies`, pinned to the version `vue-echarts` expects.\n- [ ] Move `lefthook` to `devDependencies`.\n- [ ] Keep one import path for entity types, `src/models/schema.ts`. Move the app-level constants and factories (`MITSI_STORAGE_KEY`, `BlockKey`, `BlockStatus`, `emptyMitsiState`, `newHardwareItem`) to where they belong, and delete the re-export layer.\n- [ ] Switch to SVG icons from `@quasar/extras` (e.g. `import { matDelete } from '@quasar/extras/material-icons'`, `:icon=\"matDelete\"`), pick a real icon for Scope, and drop the icon-font `extras` from `quasar.config.ts`. Keep `roboto-font` only if the design needs it.\n- [ ] Move every user-facing string into i18n. No literals next to `t()`/`$t()`.\n- [ ] Format numbers through vue-i18n `numberFormats` and `n()` (or pass the active locale) instead of a hard-coded `'en-US'`.\n- [ ] Delete the unused i18n keys.\n- [ ] Enforce the i18n rule with `@intlify/eslint-plugin-vue-i18n` (`no-raw-text`, `no-missing-keys`, `no-unused-keys`), added to the ESLint config from #39.\n\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\nLeave them. Each item is small, but the undeclared dependency breaks with a stricter install (e.g. `npm ci --legacy-peer-deps` or pnpm). The import paths and literal strings drift further with every new component.\n\n**Additional context**\nRaised in an architecture review of `dev` at `b35fc8c` (section 6). Related: #39 (lint config), #41 (underlying services removal).","files":null},{"type":2,"timestamp":1791272569,"nonce":"7cC1Fr7XQDQT+QqDQqOy1bYgfoI=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"RTE_lADOULtcMc8AAAABVIwS_88AAAAHlcnhRA","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:title":"[TASK](Frontend) Small code-health fixes: icons, texts and dependencies"},"title":"[TASK](Frontend) Small code-health fixes: icons, texts and dependencies","was":"[REFACTOR](Frontend) Declare echarts, single type import path, SVG icons, i18n-only strings"}]}